{"term":"cope","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:b4053165257d3c6a4c","definition":"To deal effectively with something, especially if difficult.","example":"Chelsea were coping comfortably as Liverpool left Luis Suarez too isolated. Steven Gerrard was also being forced to drop too deep to offer support to the beleaguered Jay Spearing and Jordan Henderson rather than add attacking potency alongside the Uruguayan.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["contend","hold it together","hack","contrive","manage"],"antonyms":["lose one's shit"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:435fbaceceb412a859","definition":"To cut and form a mitred joint in wood or metal.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c1306a225c55a1150b","definition":"To clip the beak or talons of a bird.","example":"the beak and talons should be closely coped","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:21d44a22090f6c9233","definition":"A coping mechanism or self-delusion one clings to in order to endure a hopeless situation.","example":"There was some public grousing about the number of white supremacists attempting to recruit, however; some incels argued that white supremacy was just another \"cope\"–just another self-deluding attempt to cover over the grim truth of the blackpill.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"slang","register":"slang","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:048a9e6d987872fc5f","definition":"An expression of spite towards someone who suffered a setback.","example":"\"The other guy cheated, I had no chance!\" \"Cope.\"","pos":"intj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory","register":"derogatory","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5ed5379bb6727c5b33","definition":"A contemptuous dismissal, implying that someone should deal with some problem on their own and that the speaker will not engage any further.","example":"","pos":"intj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Internet, derogatory","register":"Internet, derogatory","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:792518a310c327cc61","definition":"A long, loose cloak worn by a priest, deacon, or bishop when presiding over a ceremony other than the Mass.","example":"[…] there went firſt 160 Prieſts, all in their Copes, eight Biſhops next, […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory","register":"derogatory","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1852f57c27fb64774c","definition":"Any covering such as a canopy or a mantle.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory","register":"derogatory","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a4226243efc7e6f49d","definition":"The vault or canopy of the skies, heavens etc.","example":"the starry cope of heaven","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory, literary","register":"derogatory, literary","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:18ade7259c9e54e4c0","definition":"A covering piece on top of a wall exposed to the weather, usually made of metal, masonry, or stone, and sloped to carry off water.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory","register":"derogatory","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:25f2d3a51ad3d2b174","definition":"The top part of a sand casting mold.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory","register":"derogatory","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3348b42d6f96940218","definition":"An ancient tribute due to the lord of the soil, out of the lead mines in Derbyshire, England.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory","register":"derogatory","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:00285f5014d5817925","definition":"To cover (a joint or structure) with coping.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory","register":"derogatory, transitive","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a3ff323ebb0bdcf7ba","definition":"To form a cope or arch; to arch or bend; to bow.","example":"[W]e ſee that wreſtlers onely doe claſpe about, and imbrace one another with their armes; and the moſt part of their ſtriving one againſt another, whether it be performed by taking hold either directly or indirectly, by tripping, by coping and tugging, doe all bring them together, and enterlace them; […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory","register":"derogatory, intransitive","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9b56de511ad3b9bc4a","definition":"To bargain for; to buy.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory, obsolete","register":"derogatory, obsolete","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone","copemate","copesmate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:eeec4aa0e7d9d36088","definition":"To exchange or barter.","example":"[The Patron] Will cope with thee in reasonable wise;\nThat if the living yerely doo arise\nTo fortie pound, that then his yongest sonne\nShall twentie have, and twentie thou hast wonne.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory, obsolete","register":"derogatory, obsolete","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone","copemate","copesmate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0db39aaa0d3d8e4a16","definition":"To make return for; to requite; to repay.","example":"Three thousand ducats due unto the Jew, / We freely cope your courteous pains withal.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory, obsolete","register":"derogatory, obsolete","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone","copemate","copesmate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3c12cc6b18601030a0","definition":"To match oneself against; to meet; to encounter.","example":"I love to cope him in these sullen fits.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory, obsolete","register":"derogatory, obsolete","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone","copemate","copesmate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4af152fbac0a6d5b38","definition":"To encounter; to meet; to have to do with.","example":"Horatio, thou art e'en as just a man / As e'er my conversation coped withal.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory, obsolete","register":"derogatory, obsolete","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone","copemate","copesmate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:987ae7bac7824f83a7","definition":"To tie or sew up the mouth of a ferret used for hunting rabbits.","example":"His nimble ferrets must now become pioners for their master who coupes them, lest they should grow too fat to endure labour.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory, dialectal, obsolete","register":"derogatory, dialectal, obsolete","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone","copemate","copesmate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fb162bcb6c4b8a83d9","definition":"To silence or prevent from speaking.","example":"Well sir? how triflingly soeuer you trauers the matter, these my Philosophicall proceedings (for any thing hitherto heard) might fullie suffice to put your fantasticall fooleries to a perpetuall non-sute: were you not like to the rauenous Ferret, which rendeth in peeces whatsoeuer poore Rabbet doth come in her reach. And therefore it shall not be amisse to cope vp your lips a little, by taking foorthwith so strict a course as you shall neuer be able to contradict with all your skill: which may in this sort be verie fitly effected.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory, figuratively, obsolete","register":"derogatory, figuratively, obsolete","wordFamily":["cope and seethe","cope and stick","cope chisel","coper","cope with","coping saw","dyscopia","noncoping","uncoping","coping stone","copemate","copesmate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cope#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6b3303b01cb1b30